  "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/multivariable/14134292/assets/c018d9df9a75b6c124b1e49b9c2359a0f8c70a5322d7ce9c04e05722005e8e8e.png)\n\nA plate of mass $M$ occupies the region $D$ in  bounded by the circles ${x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=1,$ ${x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=2,$ and the lines $y=x,$ $y=-x$ in the first and fourth quadrant, as shown above. Its mass density at any point is given by $\\lambda (x,y)=\\frac{M}{{x}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}.$ Find the radius of gyration of the plate about the $y$-axis.",
